<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christian Rantzau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1614">1614</a>–<a href="/years/1663">1663</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Christian zu Rantzau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christian Rantzau was a Holstein noble and Danish statesman who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-of-denmark">Frederick III of Denmark</a> as governor of the royal parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a> and later as the leading member of his government. In 1649 he bought the district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barmstedt">Barmstedt</a> from the Duke of Holstein-Gottorp, and in 1650 the emperor raised it to the imperial County of Rantzau. He supported the introduction of absolute monarchy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> in 1660.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christian-rantzau.jpg" alt="Christian Rantzau" width="197" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Christian Hansen Vantore (1861-1928). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christian_Rantzau_(1684-1771).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
